# Claim: a Close value moved out of an owned carrier's match payload, an owned `??` unwrap, an owned match arm tail or a `^`-driven list loop has exactly one owner: its held directory stays open for the new owner after the carrier ends, and its tracer closes once, on o0, o1 and o2.
# Hand-derived: each "open" line reads the directory twice through a borrowed receiver; one "close" line per tracer, printed when its new owner ends (the moved list closes "loop a" then "loop b").
fixture: close_value_taken_from_a_payload_keeps_one_owner.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read --optimize=none run.jet
exit: 0 # o0
stdout: = close_value_taken_from_a_payload_keeps_one_owner.out # o0
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read --optimize=basic run.jet
exit: 0 # o1
stdout: = close_value_taken_from_a_payload_keeps_one_owner.out # o1
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read --optimize=full run.jet
exit: 0 # o2
stdout: = close_value_taken_from_a_payload_keeps_one_owner.out # o2
